From 2789eb2dbe100f0715080d06a2c749f4b01ba74d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Clarke <sanity@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Mar 2026 01:42:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 65/69] feat: add join event message type so new members appear
 immediately (#168)

* feat: add join event message type so new members appear immediately

When a user accepts an invitation, a join event message is now sent
atomically with their membership delta. This ensures they appear in
the member list immediately instead of only after their first chat
message. The join event also prevents post_apply_cleanup from pruning
the new member for having no messages.

The UI summarizes consecutive join events into a single line like
"Alice and Bob joined the room" or "5 people joined the room".

Closes #167

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* refactor: simplify join event code in accept_invitation

- Deduplicate ChatRoomParametersV1 construction (was built twice identically)
- Use params.owner_id() instead of manual MemberId::from(room_owner_vk)
- Inline self_id computation, removing intermediate self_vk variable
- Remove redundant first_delay variable rename in conversation.rs

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* test: add atomic join delta integration test

Tests that the exact delta produced by accept_invitation (members +
member_info + join event message) applies cleanly, passes verify(),
and survives post_apply_cleanup.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* fix: allow join events in private rooms, add time threshold to event grouping

- Exempt event messages from private room public-message rejection
  (join events contain no sensitive content)
- Add 1-hour time threshold for event grouping so joins months apart
  aren't summarized together
- Update RoomMessageBody doc comments with all content types
- Add comment explaining build_rejoin_delta as fallback for join events
- Add test: test_join_event_accepted_in_private_room

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

